## Overview

Unlike conventional machine learning workflows that train a single model for all tasks, this project constructs task-aware convolutional networks designed for individual ARC reasoning tasks.

The notebook investigates how simple convolutional architectures and handcrafted weight configurations can be used to generate ONNX models compatible with the NeuroGolf evaluation pipeline.

## Key Features

* Task-aware convolutional network generation
* Custom convolution kernel design
* Lightweight ONNX model construction
* Automatic generation of task-specific models
* ONNX model validation
* Submission archive creation (`submission.zip`)

## Workflow

* Load NeuroGolf utilities
* Define task categories
* Build task-aware convolution kernels
* Generate ONNX models
* Validate generated networks
* Export competition submission archive

